## 3. Spring Data JPA

Spring Data JPA was added to the Customer Service.

Spring Data JPA provides an abstraction over JPA and reduces the amount of repetitive persistence code required in an application.

Instead of manually writing JDBC code for every database operation, repositories can extend Spring Data interfaces such as:

```java
JpaRepository<Customer, Long>
```

This automatically provides operations such as:

```text
save()
findById()
findAll()
deleteById()
existsById()
count()
```

This will allow the Customer Service to implement database operations without writing repetitive SQL for basic CRUD operations.

---

## 4. JPA

JPA stands for Jakarta Persistence API.

JPA is a specification that defines how Java objects can be mapped to relational database tables.

JPA itself does not perform the database operations.

It defines annotations and APIs such as:

```text
@Entity
@Table
@Id
@GeneratedValue
@Column
```

Hibernate is used as the JPA implementation.

---

## 5. Hibernate

Hibernate is the ORM framework used by the Customer Service.

ORM means Object Relational Mapping.

Hibernate maps Java objects to database tables.

For example:

```text
Java
Customer.java

        ↓ Hibernate

Oracle
CUSTOMERS table
```

When the repository executes:

```java
customerRepository.findAll();
```

Hibernate can generate the required SQL, execute it against Oracle, retrieve the rows, and convert those rows into Customer Java objects.

