## 15. Dependency Injection

`CustomerRepository` is injected into `CustomerService`.

`CustomerService` is injected into `CustomerController`.

Constructor injection is used.

Conceptually:

```text
Spring Container
      |
      ├── creates CustomerRepository
      |
      ├── injects repository into CustomerService
      |
      └── injects CustomerService into CustomerController
```

This avoids manually creating dependencies with `new`.

Constructor injection makes dependencies explicit and makes components easier to test.

Because each class currently has a single constructor, Spring can perform constructor injection without requiring `@Autowired`.

