## 26. Real-Time Interview Explanation

A concise way to explain the implementation:

> In the Customer Service, I follow a layered Spring Boot architecture. The controller exposes the REST APIs and delegates requests to the service layer. The service coordinates the business logic and communicates with the repository layer. For persistence, I use Spring Data JPA repositories. JPA defines the persistence standard, while Hibernate is the ORM implementation that maps our Java Customer entity to the Oracle CUSTOMERS table and generates the required SQL. Hibernate communicates with Oracle through JDBC and the Oracle driver. This separation keeps the API, business logic, and persistence responsibilities clean and makes the application easier to maintain and test.

